        "_summary.md": "# Chain Summary: TX_BBO_XX_G5_1.0_3_v1\n\n**Generated:** 2026-05-04T00:00:00 by /edit-draft\n**Purpose:** Quick-view digest of the full authoring chain. If any field below disagrees with the final Activity Content, that's a drift signal worth investigating.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Requirements\nSource: `_pipeline/requirements.json` · `_pipeline/pia.md`\n\n- **Standard:** TEKS 5.8.B — Analyze the relationships of and conflicts among the characters.\n- **Activity Type:** Close Read | **Grade:** Grade 5\n- **Text:** \"My Rice Growing Project\" (Chapter 3, personal narrative chapter excerpt, ~706 words) + Chapter 1 businessmen scene (~115 words)\n- **PIA Tier:** Tier 1 (HIGH confidence)\n- **Long-text warning:** None\n\n## 2. Pedagogical Intent Highlights\nSource: `_pipeline/pia.md`\n\n- **Primary moves:**\n  - Identify the best line of dialogue showing the relationship between Mr. Mykawa and his colleagues (Target Task MC)\n  - Explain what that dialogue shows about the colleagues relationship (Target Task Short Answer)\n  - Infer the relationship between Mr. Mykawa and his wife from dialogue (DQ4 MC)\n  - Select evidence (dialogue passage) supporting that inference about the wife relationship (DQ5 Highlight)\n- **Supporting moves:**\n  - Interpret character intent through dialogue: what details Mr. Mykawa shows through the businessmen dialogue lines (DQs 1–3)\n  - Infer businessmen's conclusion about Mr. Mykawa from their response dialogue (DQ2)\n  - Explain what Mr. Mykawa's enthusiastic dialogue reveals about his opinion on farming (DQ3)\n- **Relationship types in play:** EVOLUTION (Ch. 1 businessmen), CO-EQUAL COLLABORATION (Mr. Mykawa–wife), HIERARCHICAL SUPPORT (Mr. Mykawa–colleagues)\n- **Assessment target:** Students select the line of dialogue best showing HIERARCHICAL SUPPORT (colleagues defer to Mr. Mykawa's leadership), then explain what it shows.\n\n## 3. Exemplars\nSource: `_pipeline/exemplars.json` · `_pipeline/pattern_synthesis.md`\n\n- **Selected:** 3 exemplars — G5_1.1_5_v1 [near], WW.G5.2.10 [near], G5_1.1_7_v1 [near]\n- **Match gate:** PASSED — near_match_or_better\n- **Cross-curriculum used:** yes — source curricula: EL Education (G5_1.1_5_v1, G5_1.1_7_v1), Wit & Wisdom (WW.G5.2.10)\n- **Search method:** index\n- **Progression strategy:** Details to Impressions (Literary Analysis)\n\n## 4. Excerpt\nSource: `_pipeline/excerpt_selection.md` · `_pipeline/excerpt_text.md`\n\n- **Scope:** Full Chapter 3 (\"My Rice Growing Project\") + Chapter 1 businessmen scene (3 paragraphs)\n- **Scope source:** Author directive (module plan specifies \"All of 'My Rice Growing Project'\") + verbatim DQs 1–3 require Ch. 1 businessmen scene\n- **Paragraphs:** 16 total — Excerpt 1 (Ch. 1, paragraphs 1–3) + Excerpt 2 (Ch. 3, paragraphs 4–16) (sequential numbering, continuous across excerpts)\n\n## 5. Final Activity\nSource: `TX_BBO_XX_G5_1.0_3_v1_Activity_Content.md` (post-edit-draft)\n\n- **Driving Questions:** 5 (3 TDQ, 1 MC, 1 Highlight)\n- **Assessment:** MC + Short Answer (TDQ Target Task ELEM, 2-part)\n- **Extension:** present\n- **Content block types used:** 1, 2, 3\n\n## 6. Validation\nSource: this edit-draft pass\n\n- **Checks fired:** 4 of 17 (Checks 7, 12h, 17a/c produced auto-fixable issues; Checks 3, 12c, PIA emphasis produced manual-review flags only)\n- **Auto-fixes applied:** 4 (NUMBERING_FORMAT_MIXED + NUMBERING_CONVENTION_WRONG: Ch. 1 renumbered 1–3, Ch. 3 renumbered 4–16, continuous sequential; OVER_WORD_LIMIT + EXCESS_QUOTES: TT Part B embedded 18-word quote removed; GRADE_INTRO_REGISTER x2: intro bubbles 1 and 2 trimmed to ≤25 words)\n- **verify_objective.py:** PASS\n- **verify_questions.py:** 4 warnings remaining (Check 1 ×3 false positives — script parses multi-line question blocks incompletely; Check 8 ×1 script gap — `highlight as answer` not in type alias table; content is correct per verify_verbatim.py PASS and distilled-patterns type mapping)\n- **Warnings surfaced in Step 6 report:** PROGRESSION_BREAK_VERBATIM_CONFLICT, GRADE_TDQ_HEAVY, EMPHASIS_IMBALANCE (all verbatim-carveout; no auto-fix possible)\n\n---\n\n## Drift signals to eyeball before accepting this draft\n\n1. Does §5's activity content respect §1's declared standard? TEKS 5.8.B = analyze relationships of/conflicts among characters. All DQs and TT directly target character relationships from dialogue. No drift detected.\n2. Do §5's question paragraph references fall within §4's paragraph range? DQ5 acceptable responses reference paragraphs 6 and 16 — both within the 1–16 range. ✓\n3. If §3 says `match_gate` FAILED, did §6 surface any relevant warnings? Match gate PASSED — no concern.\n4. Does §2's Emphasis Hierarchy show up in §5's DQ mix? PRIMARY moves covered by DQ4 + DQ5 + TT (4 questions). SUPPORTING moves covered by DQ1–DQ3 (3 questions). Supporting moves at 60% of DQ budget exceeds the 30% ceiling — flagged as EMPHASIS_IMBALANCE but overridden by Verbatim Column Rule (DQs 1–3 are module-plan verbatim and cannot be reduced). Author should confirm this balance is intentional.\n5. Any section marked \"N/A — upstream artifact missing\"? None. All upstream artifacts present.\n",
