        "_summary.md": "# Chain Summary: TX_BBO_XX_G5_1.0_4_v1\n\n**Generated:** 2026-05-04T00:00:00Z by /edit-draft\n**Purpose:** Quick-view digest of the full authoring chain. If any field below disagrees with the final Activity Content, that's a drift signal worth investigating.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Requirements\nSource: `_pipeline/requirements.json` · `_pipeline/pia.md`\n\n- **Standard:** TEKS 5.6.G; TEKS 5.8.A — TEKS 5.6.G: analyze and describe the theme of a literary text; TEKS 5.8.A: analyze how the author's use of language contributes to the meaning of a literary text\n- **Activity Type:** Close Read | **Grade:** Grade 5\n- **Text:** \"Text_Chapter 4 Becoming a Texas Landowner\" (personal narrative / memoir (first-person autobiographical), 616 words)\n- **PIA Tier:** Tier 1 (HIGH confidence)\n- **Long-text warning:** None\n\n## 2. Pedagogical Intent Highlights\nSource: `_pipeline/pia.md`\n\n- **Primary moves:**\n  - Identify a quote from Chapter 4 that shows the theme of the opportunity for success in America\n  - Copy the quote accurately (verbatim)\n  - Write an explanation connecting the quote to the theme\n- **Supporting moves:**\n  - Annotate text using Think as You Read strategy (Activity Page 4.2)\n  - Inferential discussion: \"Why do you think many of Shinpei Mykawa's neighbors had doubts about the success of his rice farm?\" (oral discussion in original lesson)\n  - Evaluative discussion questions (oral, not assessed)\n- **Relationship types in play:** HIERARCHICAL SUPPORT (quote-as-evidence to theme), CONTRAST (Mykawa's optimism vs. neighbors' skepticism)\n- **Assessment target:** Find a quote from a distinct section of Chapter 4 (not covered by DQs) that shows the theme; copy it verbatim; explain how it relates to the theme.\n\n## 3. Exemplars\nSource: `_pipeline/exemplars.json` · `_pipeline/pattern_synthesis.md`\n\n- **Selected:** 3 exemplars — G5_1.0_14 [near], G5_4.0_5 [near], G5_1.2_9 [near]\n- **Match gate:** PASSED — near_match_or_better\n- **Cross-curriculum used:** yes — source curricula: Fishtank (G5_1.0_14, G5_4.0_5), EL Education (G5_1.2_9)\n- **Search method:** index\n- **Progression strategy:** Details to Impressions (Literary Analysis)\n\n## 4. Excerpt\nSource: `_pipeline/excerpt_selection.md` · `_pipeline/excerpt_text.md`\n\n- **Scope:** Chapter 4: Becoming a Texas Landowner — full chapter\n- **Scope source:** Author-specified full chapter + teacher lesson plan scope signals (pipeline mode)\n- **Paragraphs:** 11 (sequential numbering from (1))\n\n## 5. Final Activity\nSource: `TX_BBO_XX_G5_1.0_4_v1_Activity_Content.md` (post-edit-draft)\n\n- **Driving Questions:** 3 (1 MC, 1 Highlight, 1 TDQ)\n- **Assessment:** QuickWrite (shortwrite type, single evidence — paragraphs 9 or 11)\n- **Extension:** present\n- **Content block types used:** Type 4 (intro with concept definition — 4 bubbles), Type 2 (transition — 1 bubble), Type 3 (conclusion — 2 bubbles)\n\n## 6. Validation\nSource: this edit-draft pass\n\n- **Checks fired:** 17 of 17\n- **Auto-fixes applied:** 2 (1 — Q2 question type renamed from `highlight as answer` to `highlight`; 2 — intro bubbles split to meet 25-word-per-bubble G5 limit: original 2 oversized bubbles split into 3 bubbles totaling 4 intro bubbles)\n- **verify_objective.py:** PASS\n- **verify_questions.py:** 2 warnings remaining (Check 1: unicode apostrophe false positive — verbatim DQ confirmed present by verify_verbatim.py; Check 5: script defaults to 5 DQs but module plan specifies 3 — confirmed correct by BBO-5 and curriculum_context.md)\n- **Warnings surfaced in Step 6 report:** GRADE_Q_COUNT (informational — module-plan-dictated), GRADE_TDQ_HEAVY (informational — module-plan-dictated)\n\n---\n\n## Drift signals to eyeball before accepting this draft\n\n1. Does §5's activity content respect §1's declared standard? — TEKS 5.6.G (theme analysis) drives every question. MC identifies theme; Highlight finds theme evidence; TDQ analyzes contrast; QuickWrite requires quote + explanation. Standards are respected. No drift.\n2. Do §5's question paragraph references fall within §4's paragraph range? — Q2 references paras 1-8 (within 1-11 range). QuickWrite references paras 9 or 11 (within range). No drift.\n3. If §3 says `match_gate` FAILED, did §6 surface any relevant warnings? — Match gate PASSED. No compensating warning needed.\n4. Does §2's Emphasis Hierarchy show up in §5's DQ mix? — PRIMARY moves (identify quote, copy, explain) addressed by Highlight Q2 and QuickWrite. SUPPORTING move (neighbors' doubts inference) addressed by TDQ Q3. Emphasis aligns. One minor note: only 1 highlight where exemplars suggest 3-4 — this is a curriculum-plan constraint (3-DQ total spec), not a drift signal.\n5. Any section marked \"N/A — upstream artifact missing\"? — No. All upstream artifacts present.\n",
