        "_summary.md": "# Chain Summary: TX_BBO_XX_G5_1.0_5_v1\n\n**Generated:** 2026-05-01T00:00:00 by /edit-draft\n**Purpose:** Quick-view digest of the full authoring chain. If any field below disagrees with the final Activity Content, that's a drift signal worth investigating.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Requirements\nSource: `_pipeline/requirements.json` · `_pipeline/pia.md`\n\n- **Standard:** TEKS 5.7.C; TEKS 5.10.A — TEKS 5.7.C: Use text evidence to support an appropriate response; TEKS 5.10.A: Explain the author's purpose and message within a text\n- **Activity Type:** Writing: Short Response | **Grade:** Grade 5\n- **Text:** \"Personal Narratives Reader: Shinpei Mykawa\" (personal narrative / memoir, 679 words)\n- **PIA Tier:** Tier 1 (HIGH confidence)\n- **Long-text warning:** None\n\n## 2. Pedagogical Intent Highlights\nSource: `_pipeline/pia.md`\n\n- **Primary moves:**\n  - Explain the author's purpose for writing Chapter 5, citing text evidence with paragraph number(s)\n  - Highlight key ideas that support the author's purpose across the chapter\n  - Use the short constructed response exit ticket to write a paragraph identifying author's purpose + evidence\n- **Supporting moves:**\n  - Identify character traits of Shinpei Mykawa (paragraphs 1–2) — comprehension warm-up\n  - Recall why Shinpei stopped making lists — literal comprehension entry point\n  - Identify literal facts about Shinpei's influence on the rice industry (paragraphs 4–5) — comprehension scaffolding\n  - Evaluate factors beyond Shinpei that contributed to rice farming success (paragraphs 4–5) — evaluative bridge question\n- **Relationship types in play:** HIERARCHICAL SUPPORT (throughout — Mykawa's individual story/legacy as primary cause; rice farming success, renamed station, immigrant settlement, melting pot as effects)\n- **Assessment target:** Explain the author's purpose for writing Chapter 5 (\"My Success in America\"), supporting with at least one piece of text evidence cited by paragraph number; PRIMARY moves only\n\n## 3. Exemplars\nSource: `_pipeline/exemplars.json` · `_pipeline/pattern_synthesis.md`\n\n- **Selected:** 2 exemplars — G5_2.0_2 [near], G5_1.0_2 [partial]\n- **Match gate:** PASSED — near_match_or_better\n- **Cross-curriculum used:** yes — source curriculum: Fishtank (Priority 4 fallback; no TX_BBO exemplars in catalog)\n- **Search method:** both (index + folder_browse)\n- **Progression strategy:** Details to Impressions — gather specific evidence from sequential sections → form an impression of authorial intent → synthesize into an explanatory response citing evidence\n\n## 4. Excerpt\nSource: `_pipeline/excerpt_selection.md` · `_pipeline/excerpt_text.md`\n\n- **Scope:** Full Chapter 5 — paragraphs (1)–(15), including all 6 image blocks\n- **Scope source:** Author directive — module plan explicitly specifies \"All of Chapter 5 / Include images from text\"\n- **Paragraphs:** 15 (9 prose + 6 image blocks; sequential numbering from (1))\n\n## 5. Final Activity\nSource: `TX_BBO_XX_G5_1.0_5_v1_Activity_Content.md` (post-edit-draft)\n\n- **Driving Questions:** 3 (1 LCQ, 1 TDQ, 1 Highlight) — 3-DQ budget per Bluebonnet curriculum guidance (overrides general 4-minimum)\n- **Assessment:** Short Write (single verbatim TT; no Claim question per Verbatim Atomicity Invariants and curriculum_context.md)\n- **Extension:** present\n- **Content block types used:** 1, 2, 3\n\n## 6. Validation\nSource: this edit-draft pass\n\n- **Checks fired:** 8 issues across Checks 6, 7, 9, 12, 13 (of 17 checks run)\n- **Auto-fixes applied:** 8 (details below):\n  - Priority 6 (PARA_QUALIFIER_NARROW): removed \"Based on paragraphs 5 and 6\" qualifier from Q2\n  - Priority 12 (TYPE_MISMATCH): corrected Q3 type from \"highlight as answer\" → \"highlight\"\n  - Priority 17 (CRITERIA_AND_STACK): changed \"and\" → \"or\" in Q2 criteria\n  - Priority 17 (CRITERIA over word limit): trimmed Q3 criteria from 47 to 19 words\n  - Priority 17 (CRITERIA over word limit): trimmed ShortWrite criteria from 29 to 18 words\n  - Priority 11 (OVER_WORD_LIMIT): trimmed Extension question from ~39 to ~33 words\n  - Priority 21 (GRADE_INTRO_REGISTER sub-rule a): trimmed Bubble 1 from 27 to 21 words\n  - Priority 21 (GRADE_INTRO_REGISTER sub-rule b): rewritten Bubble 2 to single sentence ≤24 words\n- **verify_objective.py:** PASS — Shinpei Mykawa present in Objective\n- **verify_questions.py:** 1 warning remaining — Check 5 (DQ count: script defaults to 5; actual count of 3 is correct per curriculum guidance override; not a real defect)\n- **Warnings surfaced in Step 6 report:** GRADE_Q_COUNT (informational — curriculum override), Claim omission (documented override per Verbatim Atomicity Invariants)\n\n---\n\n## Drift signals to eyeball before accepting this draft\n\n1. Does §5's activity content respect §1's declared standard? (TEKS 5.10.A = author's purpose; all 3 DQs scaffold toward author's purpose explanation. RL-style questions not present. Confirmed aligned.)\n2. Do §5's question paragraph references fall within §4's paragraph range? (Q1 refs para 3 ✓; Q3 refs paras 8–13 ✓; all within (1)–(15) range.)\n3. If §3 says match_gate PASSED, did §6 surface any relevant warnings? (Match gate PASSED with near-match primary exemplar. No exemplar-quality warnings in §6.)\n4. Does §2's Emphasis Hierarchy show up in §5's DQ mix? (PRIMARY: Highlight evidence of author's purpose = Q3 ✓; Explain author's purpose = ShortWrite ✓. SUPPORTING comprehension scaffolded via Q1 LCQ. No dedicated SUPPORTING question given 3-DQ budget — documented and acceptable.)\n5. Any section marked \"N/A — upstream artifact missing\"? None. All upstream artifacts present.\n",
